{
  "assembly_notes": "The staved body is the single grounded root; the hoop bands, the permanent head, the hinge lugs and pin, the bail eyelets and struts and the ear prongs and pins are all welded visuals of that part, so the only part-to-part pairs in the model are the moving members against their host. Every moving member is captured by a coaxial running fit (skirt in collar bore, knuckle on rim pin, shank in bunghole bore, stub in ear eyelet, eye on ear pin) whose clearance is invariant under that joint's own motion, so strokes are bounded by engagement length rather than by free constants. The swing bail additionally derives its arch radius from the sampled swept envelope of whichever closure is fitted, which is the one genuinely cross-slot dimension in the assembly.",
